# schemes.json (the real 1,000-scheme dataset) is deliberately tracked, not
# ignored -- audit finding H2: apps/api/tests/test_import.py,
# test_eligibility_matcher.py, test_recommendation.py, test_api_routes.py,
# and the assistant tests all skip outright when this file is absent (see
# each file's own `SCHEMES_JSON.exists()` guard), and CI's checkout has no
# other way to obtain it. Ignoring it meant CI silently ran well under half
# the test suite while still reporting green. It is public government
# scheme data, not a secret, and 2.4MB is unremarkable for git.
